# The pack payload is a BUILD artifact (4.4.0, the 2026-09-10 amendment, Task 2b): `python
# tools/build_asset_packs.py tts` places kokoro-multi-lang-v1_0.tar.bz2 here from the local mirror
# (or the upstream release), its sha256 taken on the way in against TtsModelManager's own
# KNOWN_GOOD_TAR_SHA256 literal and re-hashed out of the directory afterwards. 350 MB of model must
# never enter a repo with a public remote, and the root .gitignore's blob walls (*.so, *.dlc,
# *.context, *.bin) do not cover .tar.bz2 — so this pattern IS the wall.
#
# The wall is written as "everything in the payload directory EXCEPT the anchor" rather than as the
# archive's name: a second file added by a future layout would otherwise be committable by
# default, and everything in this directory rides into the AAB and onto every device that fetches
# the voice (the pack is untargeted — one variant, all devices).
#
# The .gitkeep is TRACKED and is the one file here that must stay visible to git: it is what proves
# the payload directory exists in a clean clone, and TtsPackLayoutTest reads the directory from the
# repo. Note the negation can only re-include a DIRECT child, which is why the wall stops at the
# payload directory's contents instead of walling src/main/assets/ wholesale.
src/main/assets/tts_kokoro/*
!src/main/assets/tts_kokoro/.gitkeep
